 "callout": "<b>Why this sits alongside the GA4 dashboard.</b> GA4 only fires for bookings made on our own website widget, so it is blind to <b>OpenTable and Resy</b>, only partly captures <b>Google Reserve</b>, and never sees walk-ins or the reservation desks, which together are the majority of USA covers. That is why the two numbers diverge: GA4 reads <b>▼19.2% YoY</b> on website bookings while total covers created across every channel are <b>▲10.2% YoY</b>. OpenTable and Resy alone move close to 900 covers a week, entirely invisible to GA4. Read covers as the fuller demand and channel picture, not as a contradiction of the GA4 story."
